WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.400
- My way of expressing myself
has always been physical.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.992
My mom told that since I was little

00:00:05.992 --> 00:00:08.251
if I would be angry or happy or whatever

00:00:08.251 --> 00:00:11.501
you would see it in my body language.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:14.251
For me having a new way
of challenging my body,

00:00:14.251 --> 00:00:17.472
a new way of pushing the
limits of what my body can do

00:00:17.472 --> 00:00:21.639
that was the thing that really
got me hooked in flying.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.010
My name is Inka Tiitto,

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:33.541
and I'm a dancer and a world
champion indoor skydiver.

00:00:33.541 --> 00:00:36.112
(bright inspirational instrument music)

00:00:36.112 --> 00:00:38.352
I started dancing when
I was three years old

00:00:38.352 --> 00:00:41.762
and as long as I remember
I've been dancing.

00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:43.843
When indoor skydiving came along

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.841
I found something for the first time

00:00:45.841 --> 00:00:47.661
that I was more passionate about

00:00:47.661 --> 00:00:49.771
than I ever was about dancing.

00:00:49.771 --> 00:00:50.891
Suddenly I realized, like,

00:00:50.891 --> 00:00:53.701
"I've just found a new way of dancing,

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:57.363
"it's just on a different
kind of dance floor."

00:00:57.363 --> 00:00:59.861
The discipline that I compete
in is called freestyle

00:00:59.861 --> 00:01:02.171
but when I'm speaking
about my flying overall

00:01:02.171 --> 00:01:04.872
I prefer to use the term air dancing,

00:01:04.872 --> 00:01:07.249
because it's not just about competing

00:01:07.249 --> 00:01:08.621
and that set discipline.

00:01:08.621 --> 00:01:10.268
It's about creating something new

00:01:10.268 --> 00:01:14.520
and exploring the limits of
what we can do in flying.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.349
And I would like to take flying

00:01:16.349 --> 00:01:20.516
from being a sport towards
being a form of performing arts.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.531
Flying for sure is way
harder than it looks like.

00:01:25.531 --> 00:01:29.329
The wind speeds can go
up to 180 miles an hour.

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:33.619
You have to be strong,
you have to be flexible.

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:35.971
A lot of the body positions look easy

00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:39.920
but they actually require a
lot to perform them nicely.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.909
So a split, for example,
it might look like

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:45.978
I'm just resting in that
flexible body position

00:01:45.978 --> 00:01:47.559
but I'm actually, all the time,

00:01:47.559 --> 00:01:50.520
pushing against the air
flow to have control.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.459
(uplifting inspiration music)

00:01:53.459 --> 00:01:56.188
I don't always like the
use of the word talented

00:01:56.188 --> 00:01:57.739
because it makes it sound like

00:01:57.739 --> 00:02:00.419
only if you have that talent before you

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:03.752
even start flying you're gonna get good.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.280
I've always been like a hard worker myself

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.988
so if I really wanna get good at AirDsomething

00:02:08.988 --> 00:02:10.979
I'm gonna do whatever it takes.

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:14.312
It just depends on how much you want it.

